  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Fund Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: Loss of lives, livelihoods and dignity are minimised.OUTCOME 1: Humanitarian responses are rapid, informed and adapted to the needs of the affected population.OUTPUT 1: Provide rapid funding to humanitarian agencies through a national civil society owned mechanism that is i) open and inclusive; ii) governed by transparent, neutral, collective decision making; and iii) responsive to humanitarian crises.OUTPUT 2: SFB members have improved understanding and capacity to i) respond to disasters; ii) access funding more directly; and iii) negotiate quality partnership.OUTPUT 3: Demonstrate the value and complement existing humanitarian preparedness and response to promote greater collaboration through advocacy, accountability and evidence-based learning.OUTPUT 4: Start Fund Bangladesh continues to grow, diversify and secure its funding base for wider initiatives under the long-term business case.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Start Fund Bangladesh (SFB) is a national rapid-response humanitarian funding mechanism managed by Start Network and funded by FCDO (UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office). SFB provides rapid, locally-led funding to under-funded humanitarian crises in Bangladesh, builds the capacity of local and national NGO members, and promotes evidence-based learning and advocacy to strengthen the humanitarian system. The project period runs from April 2025 to March 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
