  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide rapid funding to humanitarian agencies through a national civil society owned mechanism that is i) open and inclusive; ii) governed by transparent, neutral, collective decision making; and iii) responsive to humanitarian crises.</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assumptions: Assumption that enough alerts are raised and activated during this period. Agencies have access; remote areas are accessible by agencies. Secretariat capacity to support this. Members are able to work to this timeline. Funding is available for relevant alerts. Members have access to crisis-affected areas. Members have knowledge on when to trigger an alert in slow onset disasters. The team has capacity to conduct audits/spot checks. More than one member has capacity to participate. More than one member is present in the relevant area. Feedback is realistic to address at short notice and is provided with enough time to do so. Secretariat capacity is sufficient; financial monitoring and audit tool from SCI.</narrative>
   </description>
